{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>My father and my brothers, etc.</b> Meaning: as you instructed them to do. <b>And they are in the land of Goshen</b> — as you said (Genesis 45:18): ״וְאֶתְּנָה לָכֶם אֶת טוּב אֶרֶץ מִצְרָיִם״, and the land of Goshen is, in relative terms, the best of the land of Egypt for pasture of flocks. But the brothers, when they spoke before Pharaoh, did not come with the argument as you had said, but rather as supplicants seeking a good thing, and they said (Genesis 47:4): ״לָגוּר וְגוֹ׳ כִּי אֵין מִרְעֶה״ etc. See further nearby:"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:49:17.771920989Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}